{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Ashurim, Letushim, and Le'umim</b>. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 25:3), that they are heads of nations, but the translation of Onkelos (Onkelos on Genesis 25:3) does not accord with the language of Scripture. It appears to me that Onkelos understood by \"Ashurim\" the camps of caravans — wayfarers traveling from city to city, as it says, \"a caravan of Ishmaelites\" (Genesis 37:25). He derived it from the language of \"בַּאֲשֻׁרוֹ אָחֲזָה רַגְלִי\" (my foot has held to his path, Job 23:11), \"לֹא תִמְעַד אֲשׁוּרָיו\" (his steps will not slip, Psalm 37:31). And he understood by \"Letushim\" those who dwell in tents, who are scattered (נְטוּשִׁים) across the face of the earth — today they dwell in one place and tomorrow in another. For the letters lamed and nun are interchanged in many places, as with לִשְׁכָה and נִשְׁכָה (chamber), \"וַיִּפָּקְדוּ בַיּוֹם הַהוּא אֲנָשִׁים עַל הַנְּשָׁכוֹת\" (Nehemiah 12:44), and from this comes \"חֶרֶב נְטוּשָׁה\" (a drawn sword, Isaiah 21:15), which is like לְטוּשָׁה. As for \"Le'umim,\" he rendered it \"וְלִנְגָוָן\" — in the language of islands. And the word \"הָיוּ\" (they were) prompted him here, since it would have been proper to say, as it says (Genesis 10:13), \"and Mitzrayim begot Ludim and Anamim and Lehavim and Naphtuchim.\" And in Bereshit Rabbah (Genesis Rabbah 61:5), Rabbi Shemuel bar Rav Nachman said: even though we translate and say \"merchants, and carpet-traders, and heads of nations\" — they are all heads of nations. And the matter is as I have explained: the translators rendered Ashurim as traveling merchant wayfarers, and they rendered from Letushim men of wickedness whose faces are like flaming torches burning like torches, from \"לִלְטוֹשׁ אֶת מַחֲרַשְׁתּוֹ וְאֶת אֵתוֹ\" (to sharpen his plowshare and his mattock, 1 Samuel 13:20), \"יִלְטֹשׁ עֵינָיו לִי\" (he sharpens his eyes against me, Job 16:9). And Rabbi Shemuel bar Rav Nachman said that even though the custom is to translate thus, they are nothing but heads of nations — there is no descriptive epithet in them at all. And so the matter stands."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:21:44.011581535Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}